## 7. Lessons Learned

- Linux interface state and IP addressing are different from end-to-end connectivity.
- The routing table determines how outbound traffic is forwarded.
- DNS resolution must be distinguished from IP reachability.
- ICMP filtering can make ping inconclusive.
- Evidence should be collected before modifying a configuration.
- Every corrective action should be followed by a verification test.

